    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464-a3">

                <pb facs="0778" n="644" xml:id="pg644"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 635.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Coleman to Count
                            Bismarck</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            2, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">F. O. No. 376.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, chargé d’affaires <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of the
                    United States of America, has the honor to request that his excellency Count von
                    Bisrnarck-Schönhausen, imperial secretary of state for foreign affairs, will
                    permit him to avail himself of the kind mediation of the foreign office for the
                    conveyance to its destination of an appeal addressed to the royal Prussian
                    minister of finance by the consul-general of the United States at
                    Frankfort-on-the-Main, which relates to the imposition by the authorities of
                    that city of certain taxation upon income expended there by the wife of Mr.
                    Samuel R. Honey, an American citizen.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, while inclosing the appeal above referred to, avails, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapman
                            Coleman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
